e  bought in and and we're getting some  results and I imagine it was good to  actually get a lead on somebody instead  of the other way around as you've had  happened a couple of times  this year I mean that the the amount of  comebacks you've attempted and some work  and some not have have sort of been off  the charts coach and they think about  yeah my uh my parents were both very  thankful that they didn't have the  cardiac stress that that that we put  them through and some of the other games  and we joke with the players earlier in  the week about hey there's there's no  rule against winning you know via a  couple scores but it was that was a  complete win for us it was nice to go  out and you know we didn't get out of  gate great you know the first quarter we  were I think we were down three nothing  and then it just really kicked in from  there on and played played probably  three three consecutive quarters of the  best football that we've played so far  this year well you mentioned your  parents you're now three hundred and  twenty three career head coach and wins  behind your dad one of the more  legendary high school coaches in the  entire country how much of you leaned on  the coach from Central Bucks West High  School leaned on him a lot and it's it's  a very unique situation here that  there's actually three coaches on our  staff that plateform Chuck ders backs  our linebackers coach played for him in  the 70s I played for him in the 80s and  Jim O'Neill defensive coordinator played  for him in the 90s so he's figured out  everybody's email address so I think he  learned early on that that that if I  didn't pay heed to his email that he he  knows email addresses and he knows what  CC means so those guys a lot of the  emails that were meant for me as well  that is funny  Mike Pettine senior were referring to  but in terms of the type of coach that  you are who is within you a other than  your dad let's put it that way well I  mean it's a combination I mean I've  worked for some some outstanding coaches  throughout my career I played for George  Welsh Virginia I got a chance to be a  graduate assistant for Johnny majors I  was when I walked in the door and in  Baltimore  obviously Brian Billick was the head  coach but Mike Nolan was there Mike  Smith was there Rex was there just that  whole group of coaches that I was able  to work with over time I worked with  with  Pagano as well and then to go to a you  know be there for John Harbaugh's first  year and to learn from him and then end  up in New York obviously with Rex and  then then going to Buffalo to to to gain  some some real valuable experience from  Doug Marrone I mean I said I've been  very fortunate to us to have been able  to work with some some outstanding  coaches and now you enter a weak coach  where you're expected to win you now  have that label certainly with what  you've been able to do through the first  five games and you're visiting a team  that has zero wins this week how do you  approach that task well it's it's uh  it's a challenge that we want to have we  welcome that that early in the season  that when not a lot was expected from us  and and that was that's a particular set  of circumstances you have to deal with  and we always talked about dealing with  adversity and in dealing with the the  the voices outside of the building and  and the negativity and people kind of  wanting to compartmentalize us and cast  us a certain way that we didn't want to  live up to that and now now the  situation has flipped and and it's a  it's one that we're gonna have to handle  I mean it's handling and handling  prosperity is is just as important as  handling adversity so that's really been  the theme of our meetings after every  win that we've had just talked about the  overreaction that is accompanied with  every NFL game you either overreact  every when you're overreacting loss and  given how starved this city has been  this fan base has been for success